The native ABI headers are copied verbatim from air/OS Haiku commit
ef908702af (AMDGPU_HAIKU_ABI_VERSION 1 plus AMDGPU_GFX_SUBMIT_COPY).
They are MIT licensed; changes must stay synchronized with the kernel source.

amdgpu_libdrm_types.h is the public amdgpu.h from libdrm 2.4.123,
retained with its MIT license to keep Mesa's internal ac_drm_* argument types.
The Haiku backend does not link libdrm or issue Linux DRM ioctls.

This is an opt-in, root-only backend under active qualification, selected by
HAIKU_AMDGPU_DEVICE=/dev/dri/amdgpu/0 in the private EGL build. It does not
install a system renderer or imply unprivileged command safety or reset/reuse.

The backend implements private BOs, 64 GiB file-local GPU address spaces,
binary CPU synchronization and synchronous graphics submission. It copies
the preamble and main IB into one owned command buffer and signals Mesa's
fence only after the kernel's private hardware completion fence. When the
kernel advertises COPY_SUBMIT, it snapshots that outer IB into private,
read-only GPU storage. Older kernels retain the original mapped-IB path.
This does not validate nested commands or shaders or remove the root gate.
Device loss is terminal for that instance. Compute/SDMA/video queues, sharing, timeline
sync, sparse mapping, migration and reset are not advertised. Video decoding
continues through the separate native media add-on.

For command validation research, HAIKU_AMDGPU_TRACE_IB=N (1 through 256)
dumps the first N complete flattened submissions per native device to stderr,
including the preamble, main commands and padding passed to the kernel.
It is disabled by default. Captures and timings with this diagnostic enabled
are not performance qualification results. This does not validate commands.
inspect-ib-trace.py reads these captures, checks contiguous capture/packet
framing and reports observed packet and direct SET register coverage as JSON.
Its optional --export directory writes little-endian .ib files for Mesa's
ac_ib_parser polaris10. Neither tool establishes a safe command allowlist.

native_gles31_probe.cpp / run-gles31.sh exercise indexed, instanced and
indirect draws; UBO updates; depth/stencil and positive/negative queries;
transform feedback with guarded ranges; and direct/indirect SSBO compute.
All pixels and output words are independently checked. Both softpipe in QEMU
and native RadeonSI pass; this covers more commands than the compositor probe
but is not a complete GLES conformance suite.

native_bglview_probe.cpp / run-bglview.sh compile against Haiku's ordinary
system GLView.h and link the private EGL-backed libGLVND libGL. QEMU softpipe
and native RadeonSI pass fixed-function drawing, 12 swaps at three sizes,
exact GL and app_server pixels, and shared texture lifetime after closing
the creating view. ResizeTo posts FrameResized asynchronously; the probe waits
for the window thread to process that notification before drawing. Native
completion counters advance 966 to 1014 with no IRQ errors. This qualifies
the tested BGLView API and ABI path, not every OpenGL Kit method or GL feature.

Qualification checkpoint, 2026-10-11:
- Native GCC 13.3 / LLVM 20.1.8 full EGL + RadeonSI + softpipe build passes.
- Traditional GNU TLS is required (-mtls-dialect=gnu); no TLSDESC relocations.
- Standalone native_egl_probe.cpp cross-compiles with -Wall -Wextra -Werror.
- The same private library runs in Haiku QEMU: softpipe matches all 4096
  clear pixels and all 4096 compiled vertex/fragment shader pixels. Explicit
  AMD selection fails EGL initialization on the device-less VM, with no
  software substitution.
- Native WX5100 passes the same 8192 expected pixels using RadeonSI/ACO,
  including compiled vertex/fragment shaders. GPU completion fences advance
  from 2 to 10 and EOP vectors from 4 to 20 during the GL checks.
- After Mesa teardown, all 190 client jobs and 61 legacy GFX checks, both
  DMA paths and byte-exact H.264/HEVC decoder regressions pass. Combined IRQ
  counters are 200 completed fences / 400 EOPs, empty ring, zero faults.
- The kernel must initialize the actual Polaris tables (Haiku ead5796ccc).
  The backend rejects firmware's unsupported inherited table before Mesa's
  assertion. Userspace never substitutes invented hardware query values.
  The probe disables interactive debugger attachment so failures terminate.

Compositor checkpoint, same day, commit 760c04a:
- native_compositor_probe.cpp tests shared texture upload, GLSL texturing,
  scissor/alpha blending, pbuffer/default framebuffer, a worker thread with
  shared contexts, and EGL_PLATFORM_SURFACELESS_MESA.
- The first native run passed its small scene, then asserted in a pthread
  mutex. Debugger traced this to si_set_shader_buffer during a texture's
  compute metadata clear. Textures do not initialize valid_buffer_range.
  Shader-buffer and CP DMA range tracking now require PIPE_BUFFER, matching
  image range tracking, without changing texture synchronization.
- Both changed C units compile with the host Haiku cross compiler using the
  native preprocessed configuration. The full native build passes. QEMU
  softpipe passes the basic/no-device gates and every compositor scene.
- Native library 18d872ff57a9bd36f0a30761bf33527174226585b5e85c4f3a400757a73de440
  passes all 4096 small and 786432 large pixels in each of three scenes.
  Thirty draw+finish and thirty draw+readback frames per scene measure
  6.37--6.59 ms and 8.39--9.01 ms respectively on the native WX5100.
  These are probe timings, not application or display latency measurements.
- The basic gate adds two EGL setup jobs plus eight measured shader jobs;
  the compositor adds 221 jobs (fences 141 to 362, EOPs 282 to 724).
  After teardown, 190 client jobs, 61 legacy checks, both DMA paths and
  byte-exact H.264/HEVC regressions pass. Final IRQ: 552 completions/waits,
  1104 EOPs, empty ring, no faults/unknown/overflow. VNC desktop is intact.
  The host harness initially omitted the two EGL setup jobs; its counter
  assertion was corrected by inspecting the completed run, without rerunning
  rendering or resetting a successful GPU workload.

Window checkpoint, same library and kernel:
- native_window_probe.cpp runs a normal BApplication loop and renders on a
  worker thread through EGL_WINDOW_BIT and the real BitmapHook interface.
  Thirty-six swaps cover 320x192, 513x257 and 128x96 sizes, checking every
  published BGRA pixel and independent app_server screen pixels. Surface
  destruction must detach the bitmap before its owner is destroyed.
- Host cross compilation, native compilation and QEMU softpipe pass. QEMU's
  blanked desktop initially produced black screen captures; waking it allows
  the complete visible-pixel gate to pass. Keep displays awake for this test.
- Native probe 0dbf62da8fc538d36fe5d23e5a5a1fff971326f668f7587f220e6bbba5ba2967
  passes all swaps, resize and pixel checks. GPU fences advance 552 to 633,
  EOPs 1104 to 1266. Both DMA paths and 131 further bounded jobs pass; final
  counters are 764 fences/waits and 1528 EOPs, with no IRQ errors.
  A host substring count also matched the final PASS line; anchored scene
  records and follow-up checks verify the same completed run without a retry.

This qualifies private EGL shader, compositor and window probes. Window
presentation still copies GPU-rendered pixels through a CPU bitmap to the
existing app_server. Native scanout/display acceleration, applications,
broader API coverage, general performance and unprivileged command safety
remain unqualified. System defaults are unchanged.

Configure with platforms=haiku, egl=enabled, glvnd=enabled, glx=disabled,
gbm=disabled, gallium-drivers=radeonsi,softpipe, vulkan-drivers=[],
gallium-va=disabled, llvm=enabled, and a private prefix. The native build uses
libelf 0.8.13, LLVM 20.1.8 and a separate libglvnd 1.7.0 prefix. Never replace
the installed software renderer while qualifying this prototype.

Build native_egl_probe.cpp with the private EGL/GLES2 include directory and
this directory on the include path, -mtls-dialect=gnu, and -lEGL -lGLESv2 -lbe.
run-probe.sh expects the executable, prefix/lib and an absolute-path GLVND
50_mesa.json in /boot/home/wx5100/mesa-amdgpu (or HAIKU_AMDGPU_TEST_ROOT).
--hardware additionally requires the render-info kernel ABI and healthy MSI
completion counters to advance during the GL work. A renderer string alone
does not pass the probe.

Build native_compositor_probe.cpp with the same include/library paths and
-std=c++17. run-compositor.sh selects --hardware or --software in that private
prefix. Hardware mode additionally verifies healthy advancing GPU counters.

Build native_window_probe.cpp with the same paths plus
src/gallium/winsys/sw/hgl, then use run-window.sh --hardware or --software.
The test requires a visible, unobscured desktop and exits after its checks.
